   "key": "dva-q-096",
   "source": "https://www.examtopics.com/discussions/amazon/view/122607-exam-aws-certified-developer-associate-dva-c02-topic-1/",
   "number": 96,
   "question": "A developer has been asked to create an AWS Lambda function that is invoked any time updates are made to items in an Amazon DynamoDB table. The function has been created, and appropriate permissions have been added to the Lambda execution role. Amazon DynamoDB streams have been enabled for the table, but the function is still not being invoked.\n\nWhich option would enable DynamoDB table updates to invoke the Lambda function?",
   "options": [
    { "letter": "A", "text": "Change the StreamViewType parameter value to NEW_AND_OLD_IMAGES for the DynamoDB table." },
    { "letter": "B", "text": "Configure event source mapping for the Lambda function." },
    { "letter": "C", "text": "Map an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to the DynamoDB streams." },
    { "letter": "D", "text": "Increase the maximum runtime (timeout) setting of the Lambda function." }
   ],
   "answer": "B",
   "answer_verified": true,
   "community_votes": ["B (100%)"],
   "discussion": [{"poster": "albert_kuo", "content": "Selected Answer: B\\naws lambda create-event-source-mapping \\\\\\n --function-name MyLambdaFunction \\\\\\n --event-source-arn arn:aws:dynamodb:region:account-id:table/MyTable/stream/2023-01-01T12:00:00.000 \\\\\\n --batch-size 100 \\\\\\n --starting-position LATEST"}, {"poster": "65703c1", "content": "Selected Answer: B\\nB is the correct answer."}, {"poster": "KarBiswa", "content": "Selected Answer: B\\nhttps://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-ddb.html"}, {"poster": "joshnort", "content": "Selected Answer: B\\nConfigure event source mapping for the Lambda function after enabling Streams"}, {"poster": "dilleman", "content": "Selected Answer: B\\nB is the only option that makes sense here"}],
