   "community_votes": ["D (92%)", "8%"],
   "discussion": [{"poster": "MasoudK", "content": "I will go with A. You can manage all mock responses within a single API Gateway, simplifying the setup and reducing costs."}, {"poster": "65703c1", "content": "Selected Answer: D\\nD is the correct answer."}, {"poster": "Abdullah22", "content": "anyone know way the questions end by this question which is 328 and there is no rest of the 337 questions?"}, {"poster": "Abdullah22", "content": "Selected Answer: D\\nA. Response Templates for Status Code 200: While API Gateway supports response templates, simply configuring a 200 status code doesn't simulate the specific responses expected from the third-party APIs. The developer needs to define more detailed response structures to effectively test the integration logic."}, {"poster": "KarBiswa", "content": "Selected Answer: D\\nhttps://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/how-to-mock-integration.html"}],
