   "discussion": [{"poster": "tullio85", "content": "Selected Answer: B\\nI think the question should have been more specific about the size of the code. The solution D is always correct. The solutiuon B is correct if the uncompressed size is less than 512MB. In the question was not specified the size of the code. In my experience is rarely to have a micoreservice code size more 12MB."}, {"poster": "preachr", "content": "Selected Answer: B\\nIf the dependency file is too large for a Lambda layer (i.e., greater than 250 MB when compressed), store the file in an Amazon S3 bucket.\\nIn your Lambda function code, you can download the dependency file from S3 at runtime using the AWS SDK. This would ensure that the function has access to the file without exceeding Lambda's storage limits."}, {"poster": "YUICH", "content": "Selected Answer: D\\nthe answer is D"}],
