   "discussion": [{"poster": "Untamables", "content": "Selected Answer: B\\nB\\nhttps://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Install-CloudWatch-Agent.html\\nhttps://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/install-CloudWatch-Agent-on-premise.html"}, {"poster": "Dun6", "content": "Selected Answer: B\\nWe need cloudwatchagent"}, {"poster": "sumanshu", "content": "Selected Answer: B\\nA) Eliminated - Using the AWS SDK means you must write custom code to capture and send logs to CloudWatch via the PutLogEvents API. This is not automatic as mentioned in option\\n\\nB) CloudWatch agent is specifically designed for collecting logs and metrics from both AWS and on-premises environments.\\n\\nC) Eliminated - unnecessary complexity.\\n\\nD) Eliminated - unnecessarily complex and costly."}, {"poster": "Saudis", "content": "Selected Answer: B\\nhttps://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Install-CloudWatch-Agent.html"}, {"poster": "65703c1", "content": "Selected Answer: B\\nB is the correct answer."}],
